      {
        "kind": "cards",
        "items": [
          {
            "label": {
              "en": "Column vector",
              "ar": null
            },
            "value": {
              "en": "\\( \\begin{pmatrix} x \\\\ y \\end{pmatrix} \\)",
              "ar": null
            }
          },
          {
            "label": {
              "en": "Magnitude",
              "ar": null
            },
            "value": {
              "en": "\\( |\\mathbf{v}|=\\sqrt{x^{2}+y^{2}} \\)",
              "ar": null
            }
          },
          {
            "label": {
              "en": "Addition",
              "ar": null
            },
            "value": {
              "en": "add components separately",
              "ar": null
            }
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "kind": "callout",
        "style": "example",
        "label": {
          "en": "Worked example 7.A",
          "ar": null
        },
        "body": {
          "en": "<p>Reflect the point \\( (3,2) \\) in the \\( x \\)-axis.</p><p>Reflection in the \\( x \\)-axis sends \\( (x,y)\\to(x,-y) \\):</p>\\[ (3,2)\\ \\longmapsto\\ (3,-2). \\]",
          "ar": null
        }
      },
      {
        "kind": "callout",
        "style": "example",
        "label": {
          "en": "Worked example 7.B",
          "ar": null
        },
        "body": {
          "en": "<p>Find the magnitude of the vector \\( \\begin{pmatrix} 3 \\\\ 4 \\end{pmatrix} \\).</p>\\[ |\\mathbf{v}|=\\sqrt{3^{2}+4^{2}}=\\sqrt{25}=5. \\]",
          "ar": null
        }
      },
      {
        "kind": "callout",
        "style": "def",
        "label": {
          "en": "● Vector Magnitude &amp; Addition <span class=\"tier-e\">E</span>",
          "ar": null
        },
        "body": {
          "en": "The <strong>magnitude</strong> of \\(\\mathbf{a}=\\binom{x}{y}\\) is \\(|\\mathbf{a}|=\\sqrt{x^2+y^2}\\). Vectors add tip-to-tail: \\(\\overrightarrow{AC}=\\overrightarrow{AB}+\\overrightarrow{BC}\\). To find a vector path, combine known vectors (you may need to reverse direction, which negates the vector).",
          "ar": null
        }
      },
      {
        "kind": "cards",
        "items": [
          {
            "label": {
              "en": "Magnitude",
              "ar": null
            },
            "value": {
              "en": "\\(|\\mathbf{a}|=\\sqrt{x^2+y^2}\\)",
              "ar": null
            }
          },
          {
            "label": {
              "en": "Vector path",
              "ar": null
            },
            "value": {
              "en": "\\(\\overrightarrow{AC}=\\overrightarrow{AB}+\\overrightarrow{BC}\\)",
              "ar": null
            }
          },
          {
            "label": {
              "en": "Negative vector",
              "ar": null
            },
            "value": {
              "en": "\\(-\\overrightarrow{AB}=\\overrightarrow{BA}\\)",
              "ar": null
            }
          },
          {
            "label": {
              "en": "Combined transform",
              "ar": null
            },
            "value": {
              "en": "Apply right-hand transform first",
              "ar": null
            }
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "kind": "callout",
        "style": "example",
        "label": {
          "en": "Worked example 7.C — Vector path",
          "ar": null
        },
        "body": {
          "en": "<p>\\(O\\) is the origin; \\(\\overrightarrow{OA}=\\mathbf{a}\\), \\(\\overrightarrow{OB}=\\mathbf{b}\\). \\(M\\) is the midpoint of \\(AB\\). Find \\(\\overrightarrow{OM}\\).</p>\\[\\overrightarrow{OM}=\\overrightarrow{OA}+\\tfrac{1}{2}\\overrightarrow{AB}=\\mathbf{a}+\\tfrac{1}{2}(\\mathbf{b}-\\mathbf{a})=\\tfrac{1}{2}(\\mathbf{a}+\\mathbf{b}).\\]",
          "ar": null
        }
      },
      {
        "kind": "callout",
        "style": "example",
        "label": {
          "en": "Worked Example D — Euclidean Distance & Orthogonal Projection",
          "ar": null
        },
        "body": {
          "en": "A displacement has horizontal component \\( \\Delta x = 5 \\) and vertical component \\( \\Delta y = 5 \\). Find the squared magnitude \\( d^2 \\) and the area of the right triangle formed with the axes.<br><br><strong>Step-by-step Solution:</strong><br><ol><li>By the Pythagorean theorem, \\( d^2 = (5)^2 + (5)^2 = 25 + 25 = \\mathbf{50} \\).</li><li>The enclosed right-triangle area is \\( A = \\frac{1}{2}(5)(5) = \\mathbf{12.5} \\).</li></ol>",
          "ar": null
        }
      },
      {
        "kind": "practiceProblem",
        "question": {
          "en": "Find the magnitude of \\(\\mathbf{v}=\\binom{-5}{12}\\) and hence find a unit vector in the direction of \\(\\mathbf{v}\\).",
          "ar": null
        },
        "solution": {
          "en": "\\(|\\mathbf{v}|=\\sqrt{25+144}=\\sqrt{169}=13\\). Unit vector \\(=\\dfrac{1}{13}\\binom{-5}{12}\\).",
          "ar": null
        }
      },
      {
        "kind": "figure",
        "figure": {
          "type": "similar",
          "vertices": [
            [
              0,
